Faxbot: the T.38 gateway ends a V.21 preamble that carried no frame (spandsp 0.0.6).

Live over Telnyx on 5 October 2026, T.38 engine sends failed one call in two:
T.38 was agreed and the carrier's packets arrived, but the fax machine behind
the gateway never heard the answer. The carrier's T.38 began with two V.21
preambles closed by an HDLC signal end with no data (its gateway relaying an
answer that started before the switch to T.38). spandsp 0.0.6's gateway then
keeps its V.21 transmitter sending flags forever; every change queued behind
it waits. Replaying the captured T.38 packets into spandsp reproduces it every
time: no frame reaches the fax machine; with this change every DIS does, and
the calls that worked are unchanged frame for frame.

The gateway also marks the T.38 channel FAXBOT_T38_GATEWAY=engaged when it
starts, for the line 0001 logs at the end of the session.

